---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Alma-Sophia Merscher"
  description="Psychologist at LMU Munich researching loneliness, social cohesion, and how they relate to political attitudes and behavior."
>
  <section class="hero">
    {/* pre-composited onto --teal so the cutout's anti-aliased edge blends exactly into
        the hero ground. If --teal changes, regenerate this file. */}
    <img
      class="hero-figure"
      src="/images/alma-portrait-teal-640.webp"
      srcset="/images/alma-portrait-teal-320.webp 320w, /images/alma-portrait-teal-640.webp 640w"
      sizes="(max-width: 1000px) 260px, 460px"
      width="640"
      height="802"
      alt="Alma-Sophia Merscher"
      fetchpriority="high"
    />

    <div class="hero-inner">
      <h1>
        <span class="n1">Alma-Sophia</span>
        <span class="n2">Merscher</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="role">Social Psychology Researcher &amp; Speaker</p>
    </div>

    <a class="scroll-cue" href="#intro" aria-label="Skip to introduction">
      <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
    </a>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap intro" id="intro">
    <p class="lead">Welcome, and thank you for stopping by.</p>
    <p>
      I'm a psychologist, affiliated with the International Stone Center for Inequality
      Research at LMU Munich. Most of my work is about loneliness and social cohesion. I am
      interested in what pulls people apart, what holds them together, and how this shapes
      the way we think and act politically. In a second strand, I look at how stigma and
      loneliness feed into one another and how we could counter that stigma.
    </p>
    <p>
      I also run an <a href="/interest-group">international interest group</a> for
      researchers working on loneliness, and I care about getting research out of the
      journals and <a href="/engagements">into the world</a>. On{" "}
      <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/tackling-loneliness/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        Tackling Loneliness
      </a>, my LinkedIn page, I synthesize current research and open questions on
      loneliness and related topics. If any of this speaks to you, or you'd like to join
      the group, I'd love to <a href="mailto:a.merscher@lmu.de">hear</a> from you.
    </p>


    <div class="signposts">
      <a class="signpost" href="/research">
        <p class="eyebrow">Research</p>
        <h2>What I work on</h2>
        <p class="desc">Current projects and publications.</p>
      </a>
      <a class="signpost" href="/engagements">
        <p class="eyebrow">Engagements</p>
        <h2>Talks, panels &amp; media</h2>
        <p class="desc">Where to hear or read me next.</p>
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="connect">
      <a
        class="connect-card"
        href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/tackling-loneliness/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener"
      >
        <span class="badge" aria-hidden="true">in</span>
        <span class="connect-body">
          <span class="connect-title">Tackling Loneliness</span>
          <span class="connect-desc">Research and open questions</span>
        </span>
      </a>
      <a
        class="connect-card"
        href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/alma-merscher"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener"
      >
        <span class="badge" aria-hidden="true">in</span>
        <span class="connect-body">
          <span class="connect-title">Alma-Sophia Merscher</span>
          <span class="connect-desc">Connect with me directly</span>
        </span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  /* Hero: photo bleeds off the left, display type sits right of a hairline rule. */
  .hero {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    isolation: isolate;
    background: var(--teal);
    color: var(--on-teal);
    /* explicit height, not min-height: the photo is absolutely positioned so it cannot
       drive the row, and the crop is meant to bleed off the bottom edge */
    height: clamp(440px, 62vh, 580px);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.95fr) minmax(0, 1.05fr);
    align-items: stretch;
  }
  .hero-figure {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    height: 100%;
    width: auto;
    max-width: 52%;
    object-fit: contain;
    object-position: bottom left;
    pointer-events: none;
    user-select: none;
  }

  .hero-inner {
    grid-column: 2;
    grid-row: 1;
    align-self: center;
    padding: 3rem clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 4rem) 3rem clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    border-left: 1px solid var(--rule-on-teal);
  }
  .hero h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(2.3rem, 5.6vw, 4.4rem);
    line-height: 0.98;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 0 0 1.1rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    color: var(--on-teal);
  }
  .hero h1 .n1 {
    font-weight: 800;
  }
  /* the lighter half of the name picks up the accent, so the burnt orange appears
     at display size where 3.10:1 on teal is fine, rather than in small text */
  .hero h1 .n2 {
    font-weight: 300;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .role {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(0.78rem, 1.15vw, 0.95rem);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--on-teal-muted);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .scroll-cue {
    position: absolute;
    right: clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    bottom: clamp(1rem, 3vh, 2rem);
    z-index: 3;
    color: var(--on-teal-muted);
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    line-height: 1;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: transform 160ms ease, color 160ms ease;
  }
  .scroll-cue:hover,
  .scroll-cue:focus-visible {
    color: var(--accent);
    transform: translateY(3px);
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .scroll-cue,
    .hero-link {
      transition: none;
    }
    .scroll-cue:hover {
      transform: none;
    }
  }

  .intro {
    padding: 3.5rem 1.5rem 1rem;
    max-width: 720px;
  }
  .lead {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
  }
  .intro p {
    margin: 0 0 1.2rem;
  }

  /* Rounded and in their own colour, so they read as "elsewhere on the web"
     rather than as more of the site's own sections. */
  .connect {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr));
    gap: 0.9rem;
    margin-top: 1.1rem;
  }
  .connect-card {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.9rem;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--text);
    background: var(--link-card-bg);
    border: 1px solid transparent;
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 0.7rem 1.4rem 0.7rem 0.7rem;
    transition: border-color 140ms ease, transform 140ms ease;
  }
  .connect-card:hover,
  .connect-card:focus-visible {
    border-color: var(--link-card-accent);
    transform: translateY(-1px);
  }
  .badge {
    flex: none;
    width: 2.6rem;
    height: 2.6rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--link-card-accent);
    color: var(--link-card-bg);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .connect-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .connect-title {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.25;
  }
  .connect-desc {
    font-size: 0.83rem;
    color: var(--link-card-accent);
    line-height: 1.35;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .connect-card {
      transition: none;
    }
    .connect-card:hover {
      transform: none;
    }
  }

  .signposts {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(240px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }
  .signpost {
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--text);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 1.25rem;
  }
  .signpost:hover {
    border-color: var(--accent);
  }
  .signpost .eyebrow {
    color: var(--accent-deep);
  }
  .signpost h2 {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
  }
  .signpost .desc {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* Below 1000px there is no room for two columns, so stack: text first, then the
     head-and-shoulders crop. The vertical rule becomes a horizontal one. */
  @media (max-width: 1000px) {
    .hero {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: stretch;
      height: auto;
      padding: 3rem 1.5rem 0;
    }
    .hero-figure {
      position: static;
      max-width: 260px;
    }
    /* order, because <picture> is the first child in the markup but the text should lead */
    .hero-inner {
      order: 1;
      padding: 0 0 1.75rem;
      border-left: none;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule-on-teal);
    }
    .hero-figure {
      order: 2;
      height: auto;
      width: 64%;
      max-width: 260px;
      align-self: flex-end;
      margin-top: 1.5rem;
    }
    .scroll-cue {
      display: none;
    }
  }
</style>
